The Educational Society of Canada, or ESC, is the national organization for secondary school students.
Education is a powerful force to influence our future by providing knowledge and understanding that will help us succeed in life. It enables us to connect with other people and forms part of a global community. We can also change society through education. The World Bank estimates that there are 25 million youth globally who do not go on to pursue higher education. In addition, 10% of all jobs require some type of advanced degree.
Escritura and ESC have been established over the past 3 years as a non-profit, educational organisation committed to educating young Canadians about career choices and helping them get ahead at work.
We believe that:
• Career education must be compulsory from age 16 onwards;
• Students should study business courses or vocational studies;
• All courses must be free of cost, including electives which may include ICT;
• Some courses should involve employment training programmes;
• Students must be able to apply what they learn outside of the classroom;
• Teachers must be able to use their professional skills in the classroom;
• Employers need to understand career planning.
These principles underlie the background to our current programme.
